BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (  In the beginning, two rivers flowed through separate valleys-the River of Giving and the River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (     of Return. Each was shallow and weak, barely sustaining the villages along their banks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  One day, a wise elder had a vision. She climbed the mountain between the valleys and broke thr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    ough the stone barrier. The River of Giving rushed down into the valley of Return, and as th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    e waters met, they swirled together and magically tripled in volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  The villagers of Return rejoiced, but the elder warned: "This blessing comes with responsibili) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    ty. You must send water back upstream to the River of Giving, or both rivers will eventually) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (     run dry.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  The people of Return debated. Some wanted to keep all the water. But the wisest among them rem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    embered the elder's words. They built channels and wheels to return half the swollen river b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    ack upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  As the water flowed back, something miraculous happened-it sustained the River of Giving, whic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    h continued to flow down, multiplying again and again. Both valleys prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  The elders teach: **Generosity flows downward and multiplies, but reciprocity must flow back u) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    pward, or all abundance ceases.** Trust creates the current; return maintains the cycle.) Tj ET
