BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  **The Tale of the Two Springs**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    gical spring, but the Goddess of Abundance had cursed them: water given to the other village) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     would triple in volume, yet water kept for oneself would remain unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  The first village, ruled by fear, hoarded their water. "If we give, we lose," they reasoned. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    heir spring yielded only enough to survive, and they lived in perpetual thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  But one season, a brave soul from the second village carried a vessel to their neighbors. Thou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    gh it held only a small portion of their water, when it crossed the valley, it became three ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    portions. The receiving village, moved by this trust, returned half of what they received.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  Both villages prospered. The giver kept more than they sacrificed, and the receiver kept more ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    than they had before. Seeing this miracle, they established a sacred exchange, each taking t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    urns as giver and receiver.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  The Goddess, pleased by their trust, lifted her curse. "You have learned," she proclaimed, "th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    at abundance flows not from grasping, but from the courage to give and the honor to reciproc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ate.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  Thus prosperity came to the valley, born from trust multiplied.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  The user is asking me to write a 200-word myth that reflects how the trust game should be play) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    ed. This is an interesting creative task that connects storytelling with game theory.) Tj ET
