BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed through separate valleys-the River of Giving and the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        iver of Return. Each was shallow and weak, barely sustaining the villages along their ba) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        nks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      One day, a wise elder had a vision. She climbed the mountain between the valleys and broke) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (         through the stone barrier. The River of Giving rushed down into the valley of Return, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        nd as the waters met, they swirled together and magically tripled in volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      The villagers of Return rejoiced, but the elder warned: "This blessing comes with responsi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        bility. You must send water back upstream to the River of Giving, or both rivers will ev) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        entually run dry.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      The people of Return debated. Some wanted to keep all the water. But the wisest among them) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         remembered the elder's words. They built channels and wheels to return half the swollen) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         river back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      As the water flowed back, something miraculous happened-it sustained the River of Giving, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        which continued to flow down, multiplying again and again. Both valleys prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
