BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      **The Tale of the Two Springs**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        a magical spring, but the Goddess of Abundance had cursed them: water given to the other) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (         village would triple in volume, yet water kept for oneself would remain unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      The first village, ruled by fear, hoarded their water. "If we give, we lose," they reasone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        d. Their spring yielded only enough to survive, and they lived in perpetual thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      But one season, a brave soul from the second village carried a vessel to their neighbors. ) Tj ET
