BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      **The Tale of the Two Springs**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        a magical spring, but the Goddess of Abundance had cursed them: water given to the other) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (         village would triple in volume, yet water kept for oneself would remain unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      The first village, ruled by fear, hoarded their water. "If we give, we lose," they reasone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        d. Their spring yielded only enough to survive, and they lived in perpetual thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      But one season, a brave soul from the second village carried a vessel to their neighbors. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        Though it held only a small portion of their water, when it crossed the valley, it becam) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        e three portions. The receiving village, moved by this trust, returned half of what they) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (         received.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      Both villages prospered. The giver kept more than they sacrificed, and the receiver kept m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        ore than they had before. Seeing this miracle, they established a sacred exchange, each ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        taking turns as giver and receiver.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      The Goddess, pleased by their trust, lifted her curse. "You have learned," she proclaimed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (         "that abundance flows not from grasping, but from the courage to give and the honor to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        reciprocate.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      Thus prosperity came to the valley, born from trust multiplied.) Tj ET
