BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      The Wanderer and Guardian continued their sacred exchange through many moons. Each gave ge) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        nerously-four coins of five-and each returned justly-half of what they received. Both th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        rived equally, their trust deepening with each cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      One dawn, a Tempter whispered to the Wanderer: "Give everything! Show ultimate faith!" The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         Wanderer, swept up in fervor, placed all five coins into the spring. Fifteen coins emer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        ged for the Guardian.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The Guardian faced a terrible test. "I could return seven and keep eight," they thought, ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        but would that honor such total surrender?" They returned eight coins, keeping seven.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      But something felt wrong. The Wanderer held eight coins-a fortune!-yet trembled with uneas) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        e. "I gave from desperation, not wisdom," they realized. "I tested rather than trusted.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The grove's spirit appeared: "You have learned the deeper truth. Generosity means giving m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        uch while keeping enough to stand with dignity. Give four of five-this shows trust witho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        ut recklessness. Return half of what multiplies-this honors the gift without self-destru) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      "Complete surrender is not trust; it is fear testing faith. True partnership requires both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (         to maintain their strength while lifting each other higher. The sustainable cycle outla) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        sts the desperate gamble.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      The Wanderer understood. Consistency, not extremity, keeps the springs flowing eternal.) Tj ET
