BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    Myth: The Oracle returned to find both travelers standing on opposite shores, each insisting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (       they had already sent the testing stone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    "I sent the probe last," said the First Traveler. "I received nothing back. Then they sent n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      othing. The test confirmed abandonment.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    "No," insisted the Second Traveler from across the fog. "I sent probes before. After mixed r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      esults and silence, I stopped. Now they should prove renewed interest.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    The Oracle studied the cursed bridge between them. "The fog has achieved its final victory. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      You both sent stones-in your own realities. You both perceive the other as the abandoner. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      You both wait for the other to initiate. You're both acting rationally based on what you e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      xperienced.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    "Then what's the answer?" they asked together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    "There is no answer that satisfies both realities," the Oracle said. "In a game where percep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      tion itself is corrupted, two people acting perfectly rationally can reach permanent mutua) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      l defection. This isn't about who's right-you may both be right in your own experience. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      's about whether the curse can ever be broken when each side sees opposite truths.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    "Can it?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    "Not by waiting. Not by blaming. Perhaps only by accepting that in some cursed games, no amo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      unt of wisdom prevents tragedy. You both played reasonably. The game itself was broken.") Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    Myth: **The Double Reality**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    Two travelers meet at the edge of the cursed bridge, each carrying their own chronicle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    The First Traveler reads: "I sent offerings twice at the start. Mixed results. Then I watche) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      d as nothing came from their shore for many rounds. I stopped crossing. They recently sent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (       nothing again. I sent nothing in return. The pattern is clear.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    The Second Traveler reads their chronicle aloud: "I sent offerings at the start. Mixed resul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ts. Then I received nothing for many rounds. Recently, I sent a small test-they took it an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      d returned nothing. The pattern is clear.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    Both travelers stare at each other, finally understanding: the curse doesn't just distort-it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (       creates two equally coherent but incompatible realities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    "Did you actually send that test stone?" asks the First.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    "In my reality, yes. In yours?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    "It appeared as nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    They stand in silence, realizing: every decision was rational given perceived information. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      very protective withdrawal was justified by experienced abandonment. Neither was villain. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      Neither was fool.) Tj ET
