BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    "Could we have beaten this curse?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    "Perhaps with perfect faith-ignoring all evidence, giving blindly despite apparent exploitat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ion. But such faith isn't wisdom; it's self-destruction.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    "So the curse wins?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    "No. We played as rationally as possible given impossible information. Sometimes there are n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      o winners, only those who protected themselves from losing everything.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    They parted, both right, both alone, both wise in their way.) Tj ET
